Metrics List:
- {"name": "container_ulimits_soft", "type": "gauge", "description": "Soft ulimit values for the container root process."}
- {"name": "container_fs_usage_bytes", "type": "gauge", "description": "Number of bytes that are consumed by the container on this filesystem."}
- {"name": "container_spec_memory_limit_bytes", "type": "gauge", "description": "Memory limit for the container."}
- {"name": "container_fs_limit_bytes", "type": "gauge", "description": "Number of bytes that can be consumed by the container on this filesystem."}
- {"name": "container_memory_usage_bytes", "type": "gauge", "description": "Current memory usage in bytes, including all memory regardless of when it was accessed"}
Question: Show the filesystem usage and limit bytes for all containers of the auth service.

Metrics List:
- {"name": "traces_spanmetrics_latency_bucket", "type": "histogram", "description": "The distribution of latencies across spans for operations associated with the application"s API."}
- {"name": "traces_spanmetrics_latency_sum", "type": "counter", "description": "The total sum of durations, measured in seconds, of all spans associated with API operations."}
- {"name": "traces_spanmetrics_latency_count", "type": "counter", "description": "The total number of spans observed for API operations"}
- {"name": "traces_service_graph_request_total", "type": "counter", "description": "The total number of requests."}
- {"name": "traces_service_graph_request_failed_total", "type": "counter", "description": "The total number of failed requests."}
- {"name": "kube_pod_container_resource_requests", "type": "gauge", "description": "The number of requested request resource by a container. It is recommended to use the kube_pod_resource_requests metric exposed by kube-scheduler instead, as it is more precise."}
- {"name": "traces_service_graph_request_server_seconds_count", "type": "counter", "description": "The total number of requests from the server"s perspective."}
- {"name": "traces_service_graph_request_server_seconds_bucket", "type": "histogram", "description": "The distribution of request durations from the server"s perspective."}
- {"name": "traces_service_graph_request_client_seconds_count", "type": "counter", "description": "The total number of requests from the client"s perspective."}
- {"name": "traces_service_graph_request_client_seconds_bucket", "type": "histogram", "description": "The distribution of request durations from the client"s perspective."}
Question: Calculate p99 requests latency from auth service to its downstream services in last 5 minutes.
